3. INDEXING, SLICING & SELECTION
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

I. Basic Indexing — arr[index]
                   — index → integer index
                   — Accesses a single element.

II. Basic Slicing — arr[start:stop:step]
                   — start → starting index | stop → ending index (excluded) | step → increment
                   — Returns a slice of the array.

III. 2D Indexing — arr[row, column]
                  — row → row index | column → column index
                  — Accesses an element from a 2D array.

IV. 2D Slicing — arr[row_slice, column_slice]
                — row_slice → rows to select | column_slice → columns to select
                — Returns a sliced sub-array.

V. Fancy Indexing — arr[[indices]]
                   — indices → list/array of indices
                   — Selects multiple elements using integer indices.

VI. Fancy 2D Indexing — arr[row_indices, column_indices]
                        — row_indices → rows | column_indices → columns
                        — Selects multiple elements from specific positions.

VII. Boolean Indexing — arr[mask]
                        — mask → Boolean array
                        — Filters elements satisfying a condition.

VIII. Boolean Masking — arr[arr > value]
                        — condition → Boolean expression
                        — Returns elements satisfying the condition.

IX. np.where — np.where(condition)
               — condition → Boolean expression
               — Returns indices where the condition is True.

X. np.where — np.where(condition, x, y)
              — condition → Boolean expression | x → True value | y → False value
              — Selects values depending on the condition.

XI. np.take — np.take(arr, indices, axis=None)
              — indices → positions to select | axis → dimension
              — Selects elements along an axis.

XII. np.put — np.put(arr, indices, values)
              — indices → positions to replace | values → replacement values
              — Replaces elements at specified positions.

XIII. np.delete — np.delete(arr, obj, axis=None)
                  — obj → index/indices | axis → dimension
                  — Deletes elements, rows or columns.

XIV. np.insert — np.insert(arr, obj, values, axis=None)
                 — obj → insertion index | values → values to insert | axis → dimension
                 — Inserts values before the specified position.

XV. Ellipsis (...) — arr[..., index]
                     — ... → all remaining dimensions
                     — Selects across multiple dimensions without specifying every axis.

XVI. Colon (:) — arr[:]
                 — : → entire axis
                 — Selects all elements of an axis.

XVII. array.flat — arr.flat
                   — No parameters
                   — Returns a flat iterator over the array.

XVIII. array.item — arr.item(index)
                    — index → element position (optional)
                    — Returns a Python scalar from the array.

XIX. np.newaxis / None — arr[:, np.newaxis]
                         — position → where to insert new dimension
                         — Adds a new axis of length 1.

XX. np.expand_dims — np.expand_dims(arr, axis)
                     — axis → position of new axis
                     — Inserts a new dimension.

XXI. np.squeeze — np.squeeze(arr, axis=None)
                  — axis → removable dimension (optional)
                  — Removes dimensions of size 1.

XXII. np.atleast_1d — np.atleast_1d(arr)
                      — arr → input array
                      — Converts input to at least 1D.

XXIII. np.atleast_3d — np.atleast_3d(arr)
                       — arr → input array
                       — Converts input to at least 3D.

XXIV. np.moveaxis — np.moveaxis(arr, source, destination)
                    — source → original axis | destination → new axis
                    — Moves an axis to a new position.

XXV. np.swapaxes — np.swapaxes(arr, axis1, axis2)
                   — axis1 → first axis | axis2 → second axis
                   — Swaps two axes.

XXVI. np.transpose — np.transpose(arr, axes=None)
                     — axes → desired order (optional)
                     — Permutes array axes.

XXVII. array.T — arr.T
                 — No parameters
                 — Returns the transpose of an array.

XXVIII. np.diag — np.diag(arr, k=0)
                  — k → diagonal offset
                  — Extracts or creates a diagonal.

XXIX. np.diagonal — np.diagonal(arr, offset=0, axis1=0, axis2=1)
                    — offset → diagonal | axis1, axis2 → axes
                    — Returns the specified diagonal.

XXX. np.triu_indices — np.triu_indices(n, k=0)
                       — n → matrix size | k → diagonal offset
                       — Returns indices of the upper triangle.
                       
